Odic's travels took him through the Dwarvish Mines, where he
gathered many daggers from the denizens, the puzzling Sokoban, which
he solved without error, and into Medusa's patrified castle.  Odic
ended the tyrannical reign of Croesus and funded a new temple to
Mars.  After a sudden and unexpected return home to deal with the
insideous Scorpius, Odic overtook the castle at the end of
Mazes of Menace. It was there he discovered quite by accident a 
yet deeper reach of tunnels, deeper than any had known.

Carefully Odic prepared for a voyage through this Valley of the
Dead, collecting all magic scrolls, armors, and such-like he could
find.  Then he carefully decended through the Valley, removing
several demon Princes from their seats of Power, before stumbling
upon what appeared to be a series of towers.  Odic overcame the
owners, retrieving what he identified as tools of invocation.  Odic
performed the invocation, and found a temple, even so deep at this.
Before he could meet the owner of the temple, however, terrible Wizard 
of Yendor returned from his grave!  Odic faught valiently, finally
able to over take the Wizard and his menions, and finding the Amulet
of Yendor!  

Overjoyed at having the object of his quest within his grasp, Odic
rose quickly through the tunnels and passageways, past many perils
and terrors, before he stood again at the stairs to the outside.
Upon climbing, however, Odic was agast.  Another challenge stood
before him.  He was able to move through earth without trouble, but
wind pummled him mightily, and only through magical amulets and
potions did he survive.  Before moving on, the insideous Wizard
appear in dupicate and stole the Amulet as well as the beloved
Longbow of Diana.  Using the corpse of a small bird, Odic turned
both Wizards into rock and wrested his goods from the stone hands.
Neither fire nor water could stop Odic, and soon he found himself on
an Asteral Plane, with a friendly Angel beside him.  Unfamiliar with
this place, Odic moved towards a door, and stood agast then the door
opened to reveal Death himself.  Terrified, Odic ran to another
door, and there, caught between Pestilence and Death, Odic's rage
took over.  He smote them both, and stormed through several
attacking Angels and Priests to a temple.  Lo!  This temple served
Mars!  Odic fulfilled his destiny, offering the Amulet of Yendor to
his one true God.  

Thus ends the tail of Odic the Ranger Demigod. 

